    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="1119" n="1017" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg1017"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">452.11/327</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 939</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-02">November 2,
                        1935</date>.<lb/>[Received November 21.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my despatch No. 908 of
                    October 2nd, I have the honor to report that Sr. Lerroux made no reply to my
                    representations <pb facs="1120" n="1018" xml:id="pg1018"/> regarding the payment
                    of American claims in the Spanish Zone of Morroco during his short incumbency of
                    the Foreign Office.</p>
                <p>I have already taken up this question with the new Minister for Foreign Affairs,
                    Sr. Martínez de Velasco. Moreover, the Counselor of the Embassy called upon the
                    Sub-Secretary of the Ministry for Foreign Affairs two days ago and was informed
                    by him that the Ministry had that day forwarded another urgent request to the
                    Presidency of the Council of Ministers, asking that some decision be come to at
                    once. While Mr. Johnson was in his office, Sr. Aguinaga telephoned to the
                    Sub-Secretary of the Presidency and made a personal and emphatic request that
                    there be no longer delay in this matter and that Sr. Rico Avello, the High
                    Commissioner in Spanish Morocco should be required to give his long overdue
                    report.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Claude G. Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
